WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.353
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:05.292 --> 00:00:06.750
BUKOLA AYODELE:
Give me one minute,

00:00:06.750 --> 00:00:08.750
and I'll show you how
Cloud Key Management can

00:00:08.750 --> 00:00:11.700
help you manage encryption
keys on Google Cloud.

00:00:11.700 --> 00:00:15.050
Cloud Key Management allows you
to create, import, and manage

00:00:15.050 --> 00:00:18.410
cryptographic keys and perform
cryptographic operations

00:00:18.410 --> 00:00:21.620
in a single, centralized
cloud service.

00:00:21.620 --> 00:00:23.630
Cloud Key Management
allows you to centrally

00:00:23.630 --> 00:00:26.960
manage symmetrical and
asymmetrical encryption

00:00:26.960 --> 00:00:31.730
keys for your cloud services
the same way you do on-premises.

00:00:31.730 --> 00:00:34.670
You can generate, use,
rotate, and destroy

00:00:34.670 --> 00:00:36.380
these cryptographic keys.

00:00:36.380 --> 00:00:38.300
Cloud Key Management
allows you to enable

00:00:38.300 --> 00:00:43.490
hardware key security with a
Hardware Security Model, HSM.

00:00:43.490 --> 00:00:46.310
You can toggle between
software and hardware-protected

00:00:46.310 --> 00:00:48.840
encryption keys with
a press of a button.

00:00:48.840 --> 00:00:50.780
You can also encrypt
data in BigQuery,

00:00:50.780 --> 00:00:52.820
and Compute Engine,
and other services

00:00:52.820 --> 00:00:55.370
with encryption keys that
are stored and managed

00:00:55.370 --> 00:00:57.770
in a third-party key management.

00:00:57.770 --> 00:01:00.620
External Key Manager allows you
to keep your encryption keys

00:01:00.620 --> 00:01:03.290
on-prem while still
leveraging the power of cloud

00:01:03.290 --> 00:01:05.660
for compute and analytics.

00:01:05.660 --> 00:01:08.270
Cloud Key Management
is very easy to setup.

00:01:08.270 --> 00:01:11.480
You can either enable Cloud Key
Management services in Google

00:01:11.480 --> 00:01:14.630
Cloud Console or use the API.

00:01:14.630 --> 00:01:16.400
The pricing model is simple.

00:01:16.400 --> 00:01:19.130
It is a pay-as-you-go model,
and you are charged based

00:01:19.130 --> 00:01:22.310
on different products you
use in Cloud Key Management.

00:01:22.310 --> 00:01:25.100
So next time you're looking
to manage encryption keys,

00:01:25.100 --> 00:01:27.830
take a minute to look
at Cloud Key Management.

00:01:27.830 --> 00:01:32.430
To learn more, check out
cloud.google.com/security-key-management

00:01:34.610 --> 00:01:37.960
[MUSIC PLAYING]

